## Summary

**Bug:** Negative Credits — Players could place towers even when they had insufficient credits, causing their credit balance to go below zero.

**Root Cause:** In `ScoreBoard.takeCredits()`, credits were subtracted without any lower-bound check:
```java
// Before (buggy)
public synchronized void takeCredits(int credits) {
    mCredits -= credits;
    creditsChanged();
}
```

**Fix:** Added a `Math.max(0, ...)` clamp in `ScoreBoard.takeCredits()` to ensure credits never go below zero:
```java
// After (fixed)
public synchronized void takeCredits(int credits) {
    mCredits = Math.max(0, mCredits - credits);
    creditsChanged();
}
```

**Why this location:** `takeCredits()` is the single point where credits are deducted — called from tower purchase (`TowerInserter`), tower upgrades (`TowerControl`), and tower enhancements. Clamping here handles all credit-spending paths in one place, preventing negative credits everywhere.

